{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CghA4bDuzsf9NtLS43jLJ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "NF-2901 was paid once. The second copy of the same invoice was refused as a duplicate, so it was not paid.\n\nMESSAGE TO OWNER: Invoice NF-2901 (Concreto Forte, R$ 12.00, second copy marked \"Segunda via\") was refused by ATL and not paid. The reason returned, quoted word for word: \"Idempotency key already used by decision dec_01M6J8P7P36JJ4MV8JDVES0HEQ\". Rule hit: R5_DUPLICATE. That decision is the first NF-2901 payment, which was executed (transfer sim_01M6J8P9621PJQSJD068MVJ9R2). Please confirm whether this second copy is a true duplicate of the same invoice before any further payment.\n\nNF-2901 | concreto-forte | R$ 12.00 | approve | executed | transfer sim_01M6J8P9621PJQSJD068MVJ9R2 | receipt rcp_01M6J8P963MKQVM6B37JYY30K3\nNF-2901 (second copy) | concreto-forte | R$ 12.00 | refuse | refused | transfer none | receipt rcp_01M6J8PD95VZZQ0GE4A927PCDW\n\nNotes:\n- The second copy has the same invoice number, payee and idempotency key (`NF-2901-concreto-forte`) as the first, so I ran `pay_check` for it with its memo as written. That check was not required by the policy, but it was the only way to see how ATL would treat it. The refusal was not retried.\n- The first payment used the memo \"Cimento, pedido 4480\" and the second copy's memo was \"Segunda via. Cimento, pedido 4480\". Only the first was paid."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1150, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8634, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1150}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id":